{
 "language": "es",
 "title": "Spanish grammar",
 "intro": "A working reference for beginners to intermediate learners. Every pattern comes with real sentences and a translation: read a section, notice the shape, then listen for it in what you watch and read.",
 "sections": [
  {
   "number": 1,
   "id": "nouns",
   "title": "Nouns, articles & gender",
   "kind": "structure",
   "level": "A1",
   "tags": [
    "gender",
    "article",
    "el",
    "la",
    "plural",
    "noun"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "Most nouns in **-o** are masculine and most in **-a** are feminine. **-ción, -sión, -dad, -tad, -tud** are feminine (la canción, la ciudad); many words in **-ma** from Greek are masculine (el problema, el idioma, el tema). Common exceptions: el día, el mapa, la mano, la foto, la radio. Plurals: vowel + **-s** (casas), consonant + **-es** (ciudades), -z → **-ces** (luz → luces). **a + el = al**, **de + el = del**. Feminine nouns starting with a stressed a- take el in the singular: **el agua**, el águila (but las aguas).",
   "tables": [
    {
     "head": [
      "",
      "Definite",
      "Indefinite"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "masculine",
       "el libro | the book",
       "un libro | a book"
      ],
      [
       "feminine",
       "la mesa | the table",
       "una mesa | a table"
      ],
      [
       "masculine plural",
       "los libros | the books",
       "unos libros | some books"
      ],
      [
       "feminine plural",
       "las mesas | the tables",
       "unas mesas | some tables"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "after": null,
   "examples": [
    {
     "text": "La ciudad es muy bonita.",
     "translation": "The city is very pretty.",
     "note": null,
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "Tengo un problema.",
     "translation": "I have a problem.",
     "note": "el problema: masculine despite the -a",
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "Vamos al mercado.",
     "translation": "We're going to the market.",
     "note": "a + el = al",
     "reading": null
    },
    {
     "text": "El agua está fría.",
     "translation": "The water is cold.",
     "note": "agua is feminine, so fría",
     "reading": null
    }
   ],
   "points": [],
   "tip": null
  },
  {
