    "ustedes"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "The verb ending already shows who is acting, so the subject pronoun is usually left out: **Vivo en Madrid.** Say it for emphasis or contrast. In Latin America **ustedes** is the only plural \"you\"; **vosotros** is used in Spain. Usted and ustedes take the third-person verb form.",
