    "object pronouns",
    "lo",
    "la",
    "le",
    "se lo",
    "direct object",
    "indirect object"
   ],
   "rule": null,
   "text": "They go **before** a conjugated verb (Lo veo) and are **attached** to infinitives, gerunds and positive commands (quiero verlo, estoy mirándolo, ¡cómpralo!). With two pronouns, the indirect comes first (me lo das), and **le / les become se** before lo, la, los, las: **se lo doy**.",
   "tables": [
    {
     "head": [
      "",
      "Direct object",
      "Indirect object"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "me",
       "me",
       "me"
      ],
      [
       "you (tú)",
       "te",
       "te"
      ],
      [
       "him, it, you (usted, masc.)",
       "lo",
       "le"
      ],
      [
       "her, it, you (usted, fem.)",
       "la",
       "le"
      ],
      [
       "us",
       "nos",
       "nos"
      ],
      [
       "you all (vosotros)",
       "os",
       "os"
      ],
      [
       "them, you all (ustedes)",
       "los / las",
       "les"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "after": null,
